      48.0,
      559.01,
      420.04,
      614.17
    ],
    "reading_order": 20,
    "text": "0. Since there are 5 students scoring marks in the interval 0 - 10, this means that there\nare 53 – 5 = 48 students getting more than or equal to 10 marks. Continuing in the\nsame manner, we get the number of students scoring 20 or above as 48 – 3 = 45, 30 or\nabove as 45 – 4 = 41, and so on, as shown in Table 13.14.",
